window.docContents[3].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Composition.StatementModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Composition___StatementModel":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Composition › StatementModel.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 121 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nMulti-session model composition with costed reductions (Lemma 3, L3)Trusted: the statement. Read with Computational/Specifications/Game/ModelIface.lean (modelIface and KeyIndAdvantageForHandshake), Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/KeyInd1KeyReal.lean (pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal), and Computational/Specifications/Reductions/Pqxdh/StatementPqReds.lean (CompositionCostedReductions, CompositionCostedReductionFamily, and CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.ModelSecure S ℓ states Lemma 3 (label L3, proved as model_secure_costed in Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean) for the one-key real-HKDF handshake ki := SignalPqxdh.pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal S P. It asserts a budget-indexed family of ReductionDsl reductions reds : CompositionCostedReductionFamily S ℓ P C K qep decT encT (kindRed against ki and two-stage prefixRed k against single-session SM.gameR) whose syntactic step-cost, query, and block-size bounds CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded hold unconditionally in P.Under SignalPqxdh.WellFormedPrimitivesδ P (which supplies the byte-length laws for fixed-width ReductionDsl handshake simulation) and ModelAdversaryPerInstanceBounded A b qStart qs, instantiating R_e2e := reds b qStart qDR qInst yields a KeyInd adversary advK within keyIndReductionBudget S qStart b, stage-2 adversaries making at most qs k queries, and ComposedAdvantage (modelIface … ki …) A ≤ 2 · KeyIndAdvantageForHandshake S P ki advK + ∑ k < qStart, ⨆ flip, …, where each summand is the single-session SM.gameR bias of (R_e2e.prefixRed k).eval2 mixed over stage 1. Because composition stops at single-session SM.gameR, no single-session primitive or message-counter assumptions appear here.\n\n\n\ndef composedIsInstQueryL58–62 ↗#Whether a composedSpec query targets secure-messaging instance k.\n\ndef ModelAdversaryPerInstanceBoundedL64–81 ↗#Query bounds for an adversary A of G(Σ_model): bounds random-oracle, initiator, responder, total KeyInd, non-RO KeyInd, startDR (≤ S.N_send_tot and ≤ qStart), per-instance ratchet (≤ qs k for k < qStart), and total ratchet (≤ ∑ k < qStart, qs k) queries.\n\ndef ModelSecureL83–122 ↗#Multi-session model composition (Lemma 3, L3) with costed reductions over ki := SignalPqxdh.pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal S P: bounds ComposedAdvantage in G(Σ_model^ki) by twice the KeyInd advantage against ki plus the sum over promoted sessions k < qStart of the worst-flip single-session SM.gameR bias mixed over stage 1 of prefixRed k.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Composition/StatementModel.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Composition.StatementModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Composition___StatementModel"},"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.StatementPqElf/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___StatementPqElf":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli › StatementPqElf.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by no headline theorem 200 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Listed with the statement files, but no headline theorem uses it. None of its declarations is in the closure of a headline theorem of either proof. Tier 1 lists it, as the closure report does: the report lists every statement file (defaultStatementFiles in scripts/TrustedClosure.lean). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nRelocatable ELF security statement for the PQXDH CLITrusted: the statement. Defines CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecurePlaced, the top-level correctness and cryptographic security predicate instantiated at cliElfBytes in Computational/Theorems/Main.lean. Read alongside StatementPq.lean (cliPqExp, CliPqxdhAdvantage), StatementPqOomGame.lean (CliPqxdhFlagProb, CliKemFailProb), StatementPqReds.lean, and LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliBinaryPq.lean (CliPqxdhElfCorrectPlaced, Placed.cliRunPlacedSig). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md and Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md.CliPqxdhSecurityFor S ℓ ForRuns asserts cost- and query-bounded reductions (L_cli, RK, D, reds) and establishes two upper bounds in ℝ≥0∞ on CliPqxdhAdvantage for the runs selected by ForRuns: first against KeyInd1KeyRealAdvantage, and second (given the HKDF random-oracle idealization gap KeyIndRoGap, DEV-CLI16) against pqxdhKeyIndAdvantageBoundActiveδ (GapSigEufCma, KemShCr, GapDhWithSign). Both bounds include the Double Ratchet prefix sum prefixSum, the Kyber decapsulation failure term, 2 * CliKemFailProb evaluated directly on the adversary A (since adversary-chosen send randomness controls the SPQR V1 ML-KEM-768 coins), and, when exc? = some exc, 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb for excused aborts (withExcusedAbortTerm).CliPqxdhElfSecurePlaced specializes CliPqxdhSecurityFor to the relocatable ELF runner Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W under multi-block placements (mpl, mmpl) for libsignalSessionLib and VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib, with exc? := none and no .OutOfMemory hypothesis on the security clause (under the modelled 1 GiB dynamic physical-memory budget; the correctness conjunct CliPqxdhElfCorrectPlaced still permits .OutOfMemory aborts, DEV-CLI15). Code bytes, relocations, and segment layout are kernel-checked against bytes; symbol labels rest on the trusted object extractor (assumption A-LINK in Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md).Scope follows Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md: unpartnered first-message payload privacy and authentication are covered by the Auth conjunct of Lemma 1 rather than folded into this game (DEV-C5), and as in CliBinaryPq.lean, the statement excludes CPUs with AES/PMULL enabled in spqr's probe (DEV-CLI10) and subsequent calls after an accepted non-matching pre-key recv (DEV-CLI11).\n\n\n\nCanonical CLI PQXDH security proposition\n\n\n\ndef CliPqxdhExcusedAbortL71–74 ↗#Holds when i is a PQXDH-mode input (CliPqxdhInputs W) excused by exc on which run i aborts.\n\nabbrev withExcusedAbortTermL76–84 ↗#Adds 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb … (CliPqxdhExcusedAbort exc run W) to rhs when exc? = some exc, or leaves rhs unchanged when exc? = none.\n\ndef CliPqxdhSecurityForL86–160 ↗#Canonical CLI PQXDH security statement parameterized by the run quantifier ForRuns over (run, X, Wp, exc?), asserting cost- and query-bounded reductions and bounding CliPqxdhAdvantage against KeyInd1KeyRealAdvantage and (given KeyIndRoGap) pqxdhKeyIndAdvantageBoundActiveδ. Cost bounds (CliAdapterCostBounded, CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded) track both total queries qTot = b.q_total + qStart + qDR and per-kind counts (bhKindCounts b qStart qDR) separating online queries (b.q_on, qStart, qDR) from offline random-oracle queries (b.q_ro), while the KeyInd bound depends only on b_ki.q_on.\n\n\n\nRelocatable ELF security statements\n\nabbrev CliPqxdhElfSecurePlacedL175–182 ↗#Specializes CliPqxdhSecurityFor to the relocatable ELF runner Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W under placements (mpl, mmpl), with exc? := none and no .OutOfMemory hypothesis.\n\ndef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecurePlacedAtL184–190 ↗#bytes parses as an ELF image satisfying both CliPqxdhElfCorrectPlaced and CliPqxdhElfSecurePlaced at placements (mpl, mmpl).\n\ndef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecurePlacedL192–201 ↗#CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecurePlacedAt for all placements mpl of libsignalSessionLib and mmpl of VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib linked at bytes.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli/StatementPqElf.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.StatementPqElf/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___StatementPqElf"}});